     Eternal City seems to have been, like many major, modern cities, a victim
of urban sprawl.  Nolonger confined to just the city itself, there are, or have
been in the recent past, 8 linear exits from EC to other cabals, and over a
dozen trans objects, both moving and stationary.  Within the space of 3 rooms
you can walk from a bustling metropolis to a grassy hill to a castle.  Trans
objects litter the city with no logical explination as to their existance,
even in our altered state of reality.  The city seems to have lost its
cohesivemess as the centerpoint of EotL, and as the place where past,
preset, future and fantasy mesh and colide.

     Now picture this if you will .. Eternal City is actually up upon a plateau
in the centre of an island.  The sheer sides of the plateau mean that only four
or five paths can wind there way down from the city. These lead to the areas
spread around the city; to a forest, an urban area, a desert.  They also lead
to areas that link cabals more reasonable forms; to a wharf, to long bridges
stretching out across the sea, to a transdimensional airport.  Our aim is not
to remove trans objects and linear exits but to rationalise their existance.
